{"id":"G2066","lemma":"ἐσθής","transliteration":"esthēs","sayIt":"esthēs","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, feminine","gloss":"clothing","meaning":"ἐσθής, -ῆτος, ἡ\n(ἕννυμι, to clothe; hence, ἐσθής, Lk, ll with, Elz.) [in LXX: 1Es.8:71 Est.8:73, 2Ma.8:35 2Mac 11:8 * ;]\nclothing, raiment: Luk.23:11 24:4, Act.10:30 12:21, Jas.2:2-3.†\n(AS)","glosses":["clothes","robe","apparel","clothing","robes"],"count":7,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"luk-23","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"robe","kjv":"robe"}},{"chapterId":"luk-24","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"apparel"}},{"chapterId":"act-1","v":10,"renderings":{}},{"chapterId":"act-10","v":30,"renderings":{"bsb":"clothing"}},{"chapterId":"act-12","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"robes","kjv":"apparel"}},{"chapterId":"jas-2","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"clothes","kjv":"apparel"}},{"chapterId":"jas-2","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"clothes","kjv":"clothing"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Luke 23:11","note":"Herod with his soldiers humiliated him and mocked him. Dressing him in luxurious clothing, they sent him back to Pilate.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Acts 1:10","note":"While they were looking steadfastly into the sky as he went, behold, two men stood by them in white clothing,","source":"web"},{"ref":"James 2:2","note":"For if a man with a gold ring, in fine clothing, comes into your synagogue, and a poor man in filthy clothing also comes in,","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G2067","lemma":"ἔσθησις","transliteration":"esthēsis","gloss":"clothing"},{"id":"G20660","lemma":"μακροτονέω","transliteration":"makrotoneō","gloss":"to persevere"},{"id":"G20661","lemma":"μακροχρονίζω","transliteration":"makrochronizō","gloss":"long-lasting"},{"id":"G20662","lemma":"μαλακία","transliteration":"malakia","gloss":"calmness of the sea, malacia ac tranquillitas"},{"id":"G20663","lemma":"μαλακοψυχέω","transliteration":"malakopsucheō","gloss":"be cowardly"},{"id":"G20664","lemma":"μαλάκυνσις","transliteration":"malakunsis","gloss":"softening"},{"id":"G20665","lemma